@page
@model CommunityHub.Pages.Organizer.SoMeModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = Localizer["OrgSoMe.Title"].Value;
}

<div class="card">
    <h1>@Localizer["OrgSoMe.Title"]</h1>
    @if (Model.AccessDenied)
    {
        <p class="error">@Localizer["Common.OrganizersOnly"]</p>
        <p><a asp-page="/Index">@Localizer["Common.BackToHub"]</a></p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p>@Localizer["OrgSoMe.Intro"]</p>
        <p><a asp-page="/Organizer/Index">&larr; @Localizer["Common.BackToOrganizerArea"]</a></p>
    }
</div>

@if (!Model.AccessDenied)
{
    var tiles = new List<CommunityHub.Pages.Shared.HubTile>
    {
        @* §705.14a — the "graphics-release" gate key is GONE with the feature: it sent no mail and only
           hid this tile, while its name implied it governed the speaker mail (that is
           "speaker-graphics-promote", which keeps its own ring). Organizer tooling is gated by ROLE,
           so no key here — same as its neighbours. *@
        @* 🔴 §914 — SIX CARDS, DOWN FROM THIRTEEN. Operator 2026-08-06: *"this overview is too
           confusing we need to merge this into fewer"*.

           The thirteen were not thirteen features. Each § that shipped something added a card and
           none ever removed one, so the hub ended up showing THE SAME POSTS THREE TIMES (queue,
           calendar, editor) and the SAME SETUP FOUR TIMES (setup, settings, LinkedIn, assets). The
           cards described the pages we built rather than the jobs he does.

           🔒 EVERY absorbed page is still reachable, by a link on the card it merged into — a card
           removed without a route left behind is a page nobody can open, which is the §889.4
           complaint in a new place. The merges are listed on each card below. *@

        @* Absorbs: Post calendar (§835) + Edit posts (§841). All three were the same posts. *@
        new("/Organizer/SoMeQueue", "Calendar for LinkedIn Posts",
            "Every post in one list — search, filter and open any one to edit. Also the day-by-day calendar view."),

        @* 🔴 §1042 — THE POST EDITOR GETS ITS OWN CARD BACK. Operator 2026-08-10: *"i have no post
           editor"* / *"make also a link on the menu for Post Editor here"*.

           ⚠️ §914 merged "Edit posts" into the card above on the reasoning that all three views were
           "the same posts". That is true of the DATA and false of the JOB: walking 84 posts to
           approve them one at a time is a different task from finding one post in a list, and it is
           the task he does most. Merging it left the walk two clicks deep behind a card named for a
           CALENDAR, and he reported it as lost — twice.

           🔑 The §914 rule is unchanged: no page is unreachable. This adds a second route to a page
           that already had one, because a route existing is not the same as a person finding it. *@
        @* ⚠️ A PLAIN "&", never "&amp;". These strings are C# values rendered as `@t.Title`, which
           Razor HTML-ENCODES — so an entity here is encoded a second time and the organizer reads
           the literal text "&amp;" on the card (§1047). The sibling tiles on /Organizer/Logistics
           ("Speaker & order review") have always had this right. *@
        new("/Organizer/SoMePostEditor", "Post Editor — walk & approve",
            "Open posts one at a time with Previous / Next, approve or hold each, edit the wording and picture, and duplicate a post."),

        @* Absorbs: SoMe post templates (§833) + Posting frequency (§842.2). All three decide what
           the automatic posts SAY and how often they go. *@
        new("/Organizer/SoMeScheduler", "Post planner",
            "Plan the campaign across all five post types, the wording each is built from, and how often each is announced. Every post is held for your approval."),

        @* §828 — where the Type 5 words come from. *@
        new("/Organizer/EventPosts", "Event posts",
            "The general event posts you write yourself, imported from your markdown deck. CEH owns the text once imported."),

        new("/Organizer/Graphics", Localizer["Nav.OrgGraphics"].Value, Localizer["OrgSoMe.Graphics"].Value),

        @* §768: the "Designer graphics pipeline" tile is gone — §767 builds that artwork
           automatically, so there is no human build step to send anyone to. *@
        new("/Organizer/ContentStudio", Localizer["Nav.OrgContentStudio"].Value, Localizer["OrgSoMe.ContentStudio"].Value, "content-studio"),

        @* Absorbs: SoMe settings + Connect LinkedIn (§833) + Asset locations. §834 made this the
           "where do I start" page; those three ARE the starting steps, so they belong inside it. *@
        new("/Organizer/SoMeSetup", "Set up social media",
            "Start here for a new edition: connect LinkedIn, channel settings, the post footer, where brand assets live, and importing your posts."),
    };
    <partial name="_HubGrid" model="@tiles" />
}
